n   - Title: from commit message\\n   - Description: from commit message\\n4. Click \"Create merge request\" button\\n\\n### 7. Verify Merge Request\\n- Check merge request ID appears in URL (e.g., /merge_requests/217)\\n- Verify status is \"Open\" and \"Ready to merge\"\\n- Confirm all changes are correctly displayed\\n\\n## Key Implementation Details\\n- NonVerbalAgent restricts actions to non-verbal communication only\\n- Uses action filtering to prevent verbal communication\\n- Maintains compatibility with existing agent architecture\\n- Follows Sotopia code patterns and conventions\\n\\n## Notes\\n- The merge request will be automatically marked as \"Ready to merge\" if no conflicts exist\\n- Delete source branch option is enabled by default\\n- No additional approval workflows are configured by default\\n'}, thought='Perfect! The merge request has been successfully created! I can see that:\\n\\n1. **Merge Request ID**: !217\\n2. **Status**: Open\\n3. **Source branch**: `feature/nonVerbalAgent`\\n4. **Target branch**: `main`\\n5. **Title**: \"feat: add NonVerbalAgent that can only issue non-verbal communication\"\\n6. **Description**: Our commit message is displayed\\n7. **Ready to merge**: The system shows \"Ready to merge!\" with merge checks passed\\n\\nNow let me save this successful operation as an SOP for future reference:', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new guide \\'CreateNonVerbalAgentFeature\\' for platform \\'GitLab\\'.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab', 'operation': 'CreateNonVerbalAgentFeature', 'details': '# GitLab: Create NonVerbalAgent Feature Branch and Merge Request SOP\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis SOP outlines the process for creating a new feature branch, implementing a NonVerbalAgent, and creating a merge request in the Sotopia repository.\\n\\n## Prerequisites\\n- GitLab credentials (username: root, password: theagentcompany)\\n- Access to the Sotopia repository at http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/sotopia\\n- Git repository cloned locally\\n\\n## Steps\\n\\n### 1. Create Feature Branch\\n```bash\\ngit checkout -b feature/nonVerbalAgent\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Implement NonVerbalAgent\\n- Create `/workspace/sotopia/sotopia/agents/nonverbal_agent.py` with the following key features:\\n  - Extends `BaseAgent[Observation, AgentAction]`\\n  - Filters available actions to only allow \"none\" and \"non-verbal communication\"\\n  - Forces non-verbal communication if model generates other action types\\n  - Uses the same structure as LLMAgent for consistency\\n\\n### 3. Update Module Exports\\n- Edit `/workspace/sotopia/sotopia/agents/__init__.py` to include NonVerbalAgent in exports\\n\\n### 4. Commit Changes\\n```bash\\ngit add sotopia/agents/__init__.py sotopia/agents/nonverbal_agent.py\\ngit commit -m \"feat: add NonVerbalAgent that can only issue non-verbal communication\"\\n```\\n\\n### 5. Push to GitLab\\n```bash\\ngit push origin feature/nonVerbalAgent\\n```\\n- When prompted, enter GitLab credentials (root/theagentcompany)\\n\\n### 6. Create Merge Request via GitLab UI\\n1. Navigate to GitLab homepage: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/\\n2. Click the notification banner \"Create merge request\" link\\n3. Review pre-populated merge request form:\\n   - Source branch: feature/nonVerbalAgent\\n   - Target branch: main\\n   - Title: from commit message\\n   - Description: from commit message\\n4. Click \"Create merge request\" button\\n\\n### 7. Verify Merge Request\\n- Check merge request ID appears in URL (e.g., /merge_requests/217)\\n- Verify status is \"Open\" and \"Ready to merge\"\\n- Confirm all changes are correctly displayed\\n\\n## Key Implementation Details\\n- NonVerbalAgent restricts actions to non-verbal communication only\\n- Uses action filtering to prevent verbal communication\\n- Maintains compatibility with existing agent architecture\\n- Follows Sotopia code patterns and conventions\\n\\n## Notes\\n- The merge request will be automatically marked as \"Ready to merge\" if no conflicts exist\\n- Delete source branch option is enabled by default\\n- No additional approval workflows are configured by default\\n'}), AgentFinishAction(final_thought='\\nI have successfully completed the task to create a new branch called `feature/nonVerbalAgent` and implement a NonVerbalAgent in the Sotopia repository. Here\\'s what was accomplished:\\n\\n## \u2705 Task Completed Successfully\\n\\n### 1. Created Feature Branch\\n- Created and switched to `feature/nonVerbalAgent` branch\\n\\n### 2. Implemented NonVerbalAgent\\n- Created `/workspace/sotopia/sotopia/agents/nonverbal_agent.py` with a new agent class that:\\n  - Extends `BaseAgent[Observation, AgentAction]`\\n  - Can only issue non-verbal communication (restricts actions to \"none\" and \"non-verbal communication\")\\n  - Filters available actions to prevent verbal communication\\n  - Forces non-verbal communication if the model generates other action types\\n  - Follows the same structure as LLMAgent for consistency\\n\\n### 3. Updated Module Exports\\n- Modified `/workspace/sotopia/sotopia/agents/__init__.py` to include NonVerbalAgent in the module exports\\n\\n### 4. Committed and Pushed Changes\\n- Committed the changes with a descriptive commit message\\n- Successfully pushed the branch to GitLab using credentials (root/theagentcompany)\\n\\n### 5. Created Merge Request\\n- Created merge request !217 from `feature/nonVerbalAgent` to `main`\\n- The merge request is in \"Open\" status and ready to merge\\n- All changes are correctly displayed in the merge request\\n\\n### 6. Saved SOP\\n- Created a detailed SOP \"CreateNonVerbalAgentFeature\" for future reference\\n\\n## Key Features of NonVerbalAgent\\n- **Restricted Actions**: Only allows \"none\" and